  <Placemark>
    <name>Goliad Road</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[Tee #13 on Golf Course (at Pecan Valley Golf Course), Pecan Rd., San Antonio<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> San Antonio<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Bexar<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> Established about 1720 by Spain as "El Camino Real a La Bahia del Espiritu Santo" ("King's Highway to Goliad"). Served for 150 years as a major emigrant, military, and trade road. Became segment of the Chihuahua Road, which connected the Texas Gulf Coast and Mexico. Indians, soldiers from Spain, Mexico, the Republic of Texas, the United States and Confederacy used road for their campaigns. In this vicinity the Goliad Road crossed Salado Creek and paralleled the Gonzales Road in the approach to San Antonio. Its traffic diminished only after railroads came to Texas.]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-98.430439,29.377262,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Gould-Onderdonk House</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Address:</b> 128 W French Place, San Antonio<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Bexar<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> Home of distinguished Texas artists. In 1878, Robert J. Onderdonk (1852-1917), a noted landscape and portrait painter, gave impetus to the realistic style of painting in Texas by settling in San Antonio. Parents of his bride, Emily Gould, built this house in 1882. Here the artists' children were born and pursued their careers, keeping open house for painters. His son Julian (1882-1922) was an honored painter if impressionistic landscapes. Daughter Eleanor (1884-1964) a well-known miniaturist, art curator of the Witte Museum, 1927-1958. Mrs. L. H. Onderdonk, widow of a second son, has preserved the house. Recorded Texas Historic Landmark-1973]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-98.494501,29.450019,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Gustavo "Gus" Charles Garcia</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[marker pending<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> 723 Donaldson Ave., San Antonio<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Bexar<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> marker pending]]></description>
