  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>F.A. Brown Farm Home</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Address:</b> 4611 Kelton, Dallas<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Dallas<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> F. A. Brown Farm Home Situated on the Peters Colony headright granted to Calvin G. Cole in 1854, this frame Victorian farmhouse was built before 1885, when Francis Asbury Brown (1836 - 1922) purchased it along with 200 acres of farmland. His son Ernest (1868 - 1943) later occupied the residence and operated a dairy farm. Preserved by Ernest Brown's daughter and son-in-law, Anna and William T. Baker, this structure survived the urban growth that absorbed many rural homes around Dallas. RTHL 1976]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-96.8310721367492,32.8503718724018,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
