    <description><![CDATA[<b>⚠ PENDING — marker may not yet be installed at this location.</b><br/><br/>CR 265, S side between Wolf Ranch Pkwy. and Wolf Lakes Dr. Marker pending. Map dot approximate.<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> CR 265, Georgetown<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Williamson]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-97.696965,30.634336,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>David Hutcheson McFadin</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[McFadin Cemetery (a.k.a. Comanche Peak Cemetery), off Comanche Bluff Road, off FM 1331<br/><br/><b>Address:</b> 401-805 Comanche Bluff, Circleville<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Williamson<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> Served in the Texas War for Independence. Soldier at San Jacinto. Erected by the State of Texas 1962]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-97.4176005581518,30.6440985597742,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
  <Placemark>
    <name>Dog Run Log Cabin</name>
    <styleUrl>#normal</styleUrl>
    <description><![CDATA[<b>Address:</b> 675 CR 202 East, Liberty Hill<br/><br/><b>County:</b> Williamson<br/><br/><b>Marker Text:</b> Built 1851 by Wm. Williams, settler from Arkansas. Owned 1901-1956 by family of A. Buck, also from Arkansas. Wood -- cypress, oak, cedar -- and stone were cut by hand; logs are joined by wooden pegs. Solidly built rooms are separated by a "dog run." Recorded Texas Historic Landmark - 1968]]></description>
    <Point><coordinates>-97.907076,30.731888,0</coordinates></Point>
  </Placemark>
